Mechanism confirmed and it's not what the test assumed:

• The ledger stores git_hash as an 8-hex prefix (dcc72f63).
• That prefix is the start of dcc72f6329bdf46b9558365833914f83ded4fc9f = Day 205 "update learnings", ~2 days old.
• A truncated prefix resolves the moment a commit starting with it is inside the clone window — which is why it's exit 0 here (52-commit shallow clone) and fails on a shallower one.

So the old fixture pinned a property of how deep CI happened to fetch, not a property of the ledger. Fixing it with a deterministic object id:
